Assume we want to estimate the causal impact of feature adoption on account value. We can see from the visualization that feature adoption has a positive correlation with account value on average. Looking at the histogram of account value by individual accounts, it’s clear that accounts with feature adoption are scattered to the right of the distribution. Interestingly, some accounts without feature adoption are in the middle range of account value, indicating other factors are influencing account value aside from feature adoption. These other factors are called “confounders” and should be controlled to estimate an unbiased causal impact.

