Robustness Check: To evaluate the stability of the estimated causal effect, the app implements two methods:
a. Random Common Cause: Checks if adding a random confounder changes the estimate. If the new effect is close to the original, the estimate is considered stable.

b. Placebo Treatment: Checks if replacing the treatment with a random placebo yields an effect close to zero.

